assert s.count(old) == 1
s = s.replace(old, old + " Added after the critic pass: e equal to the threshold is delivered; exact ties against the reference (40 nodes, three values); a NaN position is refused; a spec threshold of 0 is refused; the tied-pair count; the dump; the division by the frames in ms per frame. `test_verdict275.py`: the rule on fake cards (bands, gains between 0.02 and 0.03, the assignment guards on the mean of the seeds, F1@1.0 and lanes found per seed, the pairing of the seeds, a lanes-found gain is no violation, no topo guard, the checks of seeds / frames / read-out). `test_qgraph_score_glue.py`: the part of `score()` that otherwise runs only on the GPU, on a toy lane with patched predictions (old call unchanged, one card per read-out, kill criterion, reproduction gate, curve, dump, `--exp` required). Mutation check of 40 hand-made mutants (scratch `temp/e275/mut.py`, tag `lcr/e275-scratch`): all caught except one equivalent mutant (the topo-guard flag of the junction call has no effect inside `verdict275`) and one memory-only (`del preds`).")
old = "the kill criterion is applied to the judged spec (threshold 0.5) only, the 0.4 spec is reported and only warns."
assert s.count(old) == 1
s = s.replace(old, old + "\n- **Critic pass (`ar-critic`, mode code) on that diff:** one blocking finding, fixed: `verdict275` carried a topo guard (topo not below the control by 0.01) that this card does not contain, which would have turned (topo inside, junction up) and (topo inside, junction inside) into CUT; the guard is out (the rule above is the written one, unchanged). Non-blocking, all taken: the reproduction against the E274 sweep is now enforced (`--repro`, stops before any card is written), `verdict275` checks seeds 0 and 1, 873 frames and the read-out of the cards, `--exp` is required with `--readouts`, a NaN position and a threshold of 0 are refused, exact ties of e are counted and the card says how they are broken, the strict radius is stated, the dump keeps the model's values, card and code names agree, results.md carries the read-out in its title. Not taken: the lane GT is re-read for every read-out (about ten passes; slower, not wrong).")
